                    insight_trust:          `Trust-based delivery: you ran the operating model the research predicts works for knowledge work — light outcome-based monitoring, real autonomy over <em>how</em>, a co-owned goal with transparency on the constraint, a reward that signalled trust rather than control, and a structural answer to the hours gap. Motivation recovered, the two routing experts stayed, and 1 December is genuinely defensible.`,
                    insight_control:        `Control trap: surveillance and coercion aimed at de-risking delivery manufactured the risk. Engineers optimised for visible activity, intrinsic motivation was capped below 60 and effective velocity fell — the very controls meant to make the deadline more likely made it less likely. This is the headline lesson of the dial.`,
                    insight_crowding:       `Crowded-out drive: the full performance-contingent bonus, adopted as control rather than a share of the upside, crowded out the intrinsic motivation your senior engineers run on. The 660 000 kr bought resentment, not hours — exactly Kuvaas's finding for complex knowledge work.`,
                    insight_concentration:  `Concentration risk: routing knowledge sat in two heads and you managed the average instead of the tail. With both experts near the exit, losing one cost 4–5 months of velocity and put the deadline out of reach regardless of any dashboard.`,
                    insight_abdication:     `Autonomy as abdication: you granted full autonomy with no co-owned goal and no transparency on the constraint — “you're trusted, figure it out” — and the critical routing path drifted. Trust isn't the absence of structure; the enabling band of the inverted-U is a clear shared goal <em>plus</em> autonomy over how.`,
                    insight_abdication_tail: `Velocity stayed capped because direction was missing: a self-organising squad still needs a co-owned commitment and transparency on the deadline to stay on the critical path. You gave freedom but withheld the shared goal that turns freedom into delivery.`,
                    insight_planning:       `Planning dodged: you used motivation and pay levers to avoid the capacity-and-scope decision the 800-hour gap demanded. No bonus creates hours; the gap stayed open and delivery probability stayed capped — motivation can't substitute for planning.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed result: parts of the operating model landed, but monitoring, pay, autonomy and the gap response didn't fully reinforce each other — enough seams for the board to question whether 1 December is safe.`,
                    insight_engineer_lost:  `You lost a routing expert: flight risk crossed 40% and one of the two walked. That converts directly into 4–5 months of lost velocity and a NOK 1,1 million replacement — flight risk and motivation were the leading indicators that would have warned you in time.`,
                    insight_surveillance:   `Surveillance left a permanent mark: once activity monitoring was imposed, motivation could not recover above the floor and velocity stayed capped. Trust, once broken by being watched, doesn't rebuild inside the same project.`,
                    insight_bonus:          `The contingent bonus left a permanent mark: framed as control, it capped motivation and trust for the rest of the build. The lesson isn't “never pay” — it's that the meaning of the money matters more than the amount.`,
                    insight_gap:            `The hours gap was never honestly closed: focus, scope and capacity were the only real levers, and leaving the 800 hours open kept delivery probability capped no matter how the team felt.`,
                    insight_happy_late:     `A motivated, trusting team — but still behind: you protected the people and the relationship without fully closing the structural gap. Trust enables delivery; it doesn't replace the scope-and-capacity decision.`,

                    hint_engineer_lost:     `A routing expert has walked — the deadline is now capped regardless of the dials. Rebuild trust fast and renegotiate scope honestly before the second one follows.`,
                    hint_surveillance:      `You're running surveillance — motivation is floored and velocity capped because engineers optimise for visible activity. Dial monitoring down to outcome-based and give autonomy back.`,
                    hint_flight:            `Key-engineer flight risk is dangerously high. Targeted stay-conversations and a growth path for the two routing experts now, before one crosses 40% and walks.`,
                    hint_crowding:          `The contingent bonus is crowding out intrinsic drive. Reframe it as a share of the upside, or shift to non-contingent recognition, before resentment hardens.`,
